Practice gratitude
Effective ways to cultivate gratitude:
Keep a daily gratitude journal
Recognize the good in your life (big and small)
Focus on good intentions when receiving gifts
Write a gratitude letter to someone important


Examine your thoughts
Implement positive affirmations
Write down affirmations that are credible and achievable
Use affirmations to turn negative thoughts into positive thoughts

Examine your thoughts (Mayo Clinic, 2021)
Put positive thinking into practice
Negative self talk	 Positive thinking
I’ve never done it before.----It’s an opportunity to learn something new.
It’s too complicated.   ----I’ll tackle it from a different angle.
There’s no way it will work. ---- I can try to make it work.
It’s too much of a change. --- Let’s take a chance.
I’m not going to get any better at this.    =====  I’ll give it another try.

Examine your thoughts
Uncover negative thinking traps

Am I seeing the situation as all or nothing?
Am I predicting the future?
Am I imagining the worst thing that could happen?
Am I ignoring the positive or potential solutions?
Am I only focused on the problems?
Am I expecting unrealistic results from myself or others?


